        sec('constraints', 'Where grid capacity constrains data centres in India',
            p('Data centre capacity is still under 1% of India’s installed power capacity, according to the government, but it is concentrated. Structure Research reports that committed and under-construction data centre capacity in Navi Mumbai is approaching the roughly 6 GW of grid capacity MSEDCL allocated there, pushing new builds towards Panvel, Taloja and Rasayani. Crisil Ratings estimates, as reported by Deccan Herald, that by FY2030 data centre capacity could equal about 60% of Mumbai’s current peak demand and about 80% of Visakhapatnam’s.', 'pib-cap', 'structure', 'crisil-dh'),
            p('The Central Electricity Authority has asked states including Maharashtra, Andhra Pradesh, Telangana and Tamil Nadu to enhance resource adequacy for data centre demand, ThePrint reported in April 2026. The head of TGSPDCL, one of Telangana’s two discoms, told ThePrint that data centres need transmission lines of 132 kV and above.', 'theprint-cea'),
            POWER_LINKS),
