        faq('How much does electricity cost a data centre in India?', 'It depends on the state and tariff category: TNERC set ₹7.50/kWh plus ₹608/kVA a month for Tamil Nadu from July 2025. Uttar Pradesh charges ₹6.10 to ₹7.10/kVAh plus ₹270 to ₹300/kVA for 2026-27, and Telangana’s FY 2024-25 order set ₹6.65 to ₹7.65/kVAh plus ₹500/kVA for HT industry. Fuel adjustment, duty and taxes are extra.', 'tnerc', 'uperc', 'tgerc-rst'),
        faq('Are data centres industrial consumers for electricity in India?', 'In Maharashtra, yes: the MERC tariff order names them as industrial. Tamil Nadu bills them under HT-I as IT services, and Uttar Pradesh under the HV-2 industrial category for notified IT units.', 'merc-myt', 'tnerc', 'uperc'),
